[32m+[m[32mOnly domains that are not handled by deterministic classifiers reach Ollama.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Classifier Pipeline[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mClassifiers implement `engine.classifiers.base.BaseClassifier`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCurrent order:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. `RuleEngine`[m
[32m+[m[32m   Handles known safe infrastructure such as localhost, `.local`, `.home.arpa`, and reverse DNS lookup domains.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m2. `HeuristicsEngine`[m
[32m+[m[32m   Scores suspicious patterns such as punycode, long domains, high entropy, suspicious TLDs, phishing keywords, repeated hyphens, deep subdomains, random-looking hostnames, and high query frequency.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m3. `AIClassifier`[m
[32m+[m[32m   Uses Ollama for domains that remain unknown after deterministic checks.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Database[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe main database is configured by `PIHOLE_AI_EVENTS_DB` and defaults to:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mdata/events.db[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTables:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `events`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `domain_memory`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `analysis`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `app_state`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `action_audit`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `domain_rules`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `domain_reputation`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe collector stores the last processed Pi-hole query ID in `app_state` as:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mcollector.last_query_id[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Analysis Cache[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAnalysis results include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `risk`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `confidence`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `category`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `reason`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `model`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `analyzed_at`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCache policy:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `confidence > 0` and not expired means the cache entry is reused.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `confidence == 0` is treated as retryable.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `PIHOLE_AI_CACHE_TTL` controls expiration in seconds.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `PIHOLE_AI_CACHE_TTL=0` disables expiration for positive-confidence entries.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis prevents temporary Ollama failures from permanently caching `unknown` results.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Action Policy[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAfter a fresh analysis is saved, the engine applies a small action policy and records the decision in `action_audit`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDefault behavior is dry-run:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mPIHOLE_AI_ACTION_MODE=dry-run[m
[32m+[m[32mPIHOLE_AI_ALERT_THRESHOLD=50[m
[32m+[m[32mPIHOLE_AI_HIGH_RISK_THRESHOLD=70[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mModes:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `off`: do not create action decisions[m
[32m+[m[32m- `dry-run`: audit alerts and suggested blocks without changing DNS behavior[m
[32m+[m[32m- `block`: write high-risk domains to the local blocklist helper[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDry-run decisions use:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `alert` for risk at or above `PIHOLE_AI_ALERT_THRESHOLD`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `suggest_block` for risk at or above `PIHOLE_AI_HIGH_RISK_THRESHOLD`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `review` for zero-confidence analysis results[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mManual rules are checked before risk thresholds:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `allow` rules suppress alert/block suggestions for that domain[m
[32m+[m[32m- `block` rules are recorded as explicit rule matches[m
[32m+[m[32m- `pihole-ai rules block --apply` also writes the domain to the local blocklist helper[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Local Learning[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPiHole-AI can build a local reputation list from observed DNS history:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mpihole-ai learn[m
[32m+[m[32mpihole-ai learn --limit 1000 --min-score 60[m
[32m+[m[32mpihole-ai learn --no-audit[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLearning updates `domain_reputation` and can create learned `alert` or `suggest_block` audit records. It does not block domains automatically.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCurrent learning signals include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- query volume[m
[32m+[m[32m- recent query spikes[m
[32m+[m[32m- multi-device visibility[m
[32m+[m[32m- previous analysis risk[m
[32m+[m[32m- previous action audit suggestions[m
[32m+[m[32m- entropy and suspicious TLDs[m
[32m+[m[32m- manual allow/block rules[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Categories[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCanonical categories are defined in `engine.models.DomainCategory`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `benign`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `infrastructure`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `advertising`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `analytics`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `tracking`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `suspicious`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `malware`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `phishing`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `command-and-control`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `unknown`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAI responses are rejected if they use categories outside this set.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Ollama[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe AI fallback uses the local Ollama Python client.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDefault settings:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mPIHOLE_AI_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434[m
[32m+[m[32mPIHOLE_AI_OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:1b[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf Ollama is unavailable, the AI classifier returns a safe fallback result:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mrisk=50[m
[32m+[m[32mconfidence=0[m
[32m+[m[32mcategory=unknown[m
[32m+[m[32mreason="AI backend unavailable."[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe engine saves the fallback and marks the domain processed, but because confidence is `0`, the cache entry is retried later.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Dashboard And API[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe dashboard is served by Flask from `ui/dashboard.py`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDefault port:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mPIHOLE_AI_DASHBOARD_PORT=8080[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRun:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m ui.dashboard[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEndpoints:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/stats`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/events`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/analysis`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/devices`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/actions`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/rules`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `POST /api/rules`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `DELETE /api/rules/<domain>`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/health`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /data`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`/data` is kept as a compatibility route.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUseful query parameters:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `limit`: maximum rows to return, clamped between 1 and 500[m
[32m+[m[32m- `q`: search domains and/or devices[m
[32m+[m[32m- `processed`: `0` or `1`, supported by `/api/events`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `min_risk`: minimum risk score, supported by `/api/analysis`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `category`: exact category, supported by `/api/analysis`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `action`: exact action, supported by `/api/actions`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `status`: exact status, supported by `/api/actions`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `decision`: exact rule decision, supported by `/api/rules`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `ollama`: `1`, supported by `/api/health` to include Ollama status[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe dashboard can promote action audit entries into manual `allow` or `block` rules and remove active rules.[m
[32m+[m
